  "summary_en": "US federal regulation (23 CFR Part 630) on preconstruction procedures for Federal-aid highway projects: project authorization and agreements, plans/specifications/estimates, geodetic surveys, advance construction, work zone safety and mobility, and temporary traffic control devices. Only incidental mentions of drone radar and automated flagger devices; not AI governance.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "States must obtain FHWA authorization to proceed and execute project agreements before Federal-aid work.",
   "States must adopt work zone safety and mobility policies and perform programmatic reviews every 5 years.",
   "Significant projects require Transportation Management Plans including TTC, operations and public outreach components.",
   "Positive protection devices required in high-speed work zones lacking worker escape routes unless an engineering study determines otherwise.",
   "Compliance dates: policies updated by Dec 31, 2025 and implemented by Dec 31, 2026."
